---
description: Never show technical API errors to players (Horus-aligned)
globs: src/**/*.{ts,tsx}
alwaysApply: true
---

# User-facing errors (Horus pattern)

Players must never see raw transport/debug text.

## Do not show in UI
- Timeout ms (`timed out after 8000ms`)
- HTTP status phrases (`failed with status 500`)
- Env var names, stack traces, `AbortError`, Axios codes
- Internal exception class names

## Do instead
- Log the full error with `console.error` / future Sentry (`debugMessage`, `cause`, `status`)
- Render only localized product copy via `toUserFacingMessage(error, fallback)` from `shared/lib/api/userFacingError`
- Prefer API `message` when the server intentionally sent domain/validation copy
- Map transport failures to `errors.timeout` / `errors.offline` / `errors.server` / `errors.generic`

```ts
// ❌ BAD — leaks transport details
setError(error instanceof ApiError ? error.message : 'Failed')

// ✅ GOOD
setError(toUserFacingMessage(error, t('errors:catalogLoad')))
```

## API client contract
- `ApiError.message` is always safe for UI
- Put technical detail in `ApiError.debugMessage` / `cause` only
- `kind: 'aborted'` must not flash an error toast/banner

## Reference
Horus: `useErrorHandler` + Global toast + API envelope allowlist `{message,code,errors}`.
